<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George of Poděbrady</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1420">1420</a>–<a href="/years/1471">1471</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as George of Kunštát and Poděbrady</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George of Poděbrady was a Utraquist Hussite nobleman who governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> as regent for Ladislaus the Posthumous and was elected king in 1458. He created the County of Kladsko in 1459 and acquired the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ziebice">Ziębice</a> for his family. He proposed a league of Christian rulers to keep the peace, but the pope condemned him as a heretic, and from 1468 until his death he fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matthias-corvinus">Matthias Corvinus</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-of-podebrady.jpg" alt="George of Poděbrady" width="274" height="370" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Georg_of_Podebrady.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
